<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tagdemt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tagdemt is a site near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiaret">Tiaret</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, beside the remains of the medieval Rustamid capital Tahert. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir-abdelkader">Emir Abdelkader</a> made it his capital in the late 1830s, building a fortress, arsenal and mint there to give his state a base beyond the reach of French columns. French troops under Bugeaud took and destroyed it in 1841.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tagdemt.jpg" alt="Tagdemt" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vikoula5 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dz_-_14_-_Tagdemt.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
